    "explanation": "To both parties: the 36.30 SGD fare dispute is decided under the route-deviation matrix (POL-RD-24), the deviation measure (POL-RD-22) and the traffic-justification rule (POL-RD-23).\n\nWhat the record establishes. The platform trip record (EV-TRIP-05010, status COMPLETE, weight 1.0) records 22.0 km driven against a recommended-route distance of 19.7 km — a 2.30 km deviation, above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05010, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) shows which route was taken: Airport Boulevard, then the Pan-Island Expressway from 14:36:50, then Sims Way, Lavender Street and Victoria Street; the recommended East Coast Parkway was not driven. The trip record's own events mark the departure at the Airport Boulevard / PIE-ECP split at 14:36:54 and the rejoin at Victoria Street / Lavender Street at 14:58:48. The LTA advisory for the recommended ECP segment, overlapping the trip window (EV-ADVIS-05010-01, COMPLETE, weight 1.0), is type NONE, speed bands 5–7, recording no incident, roadwork or closure, so POL-RD-23 is not satisfied and the reroute is not traffic-justified. The driver's statement that 'ECP sometimes jam near Marina' is exactly the bare assertion POL-RD-23 says cannot justify a reroute without the data, so it does not.\n\nWhich row applies. Not traffic-justified with a deviation over 1 km is row (d) of POL-RD-24: refund of the excess distance fare in full. The rider was also not informed — the chat log (EV-CHAT-05010, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) holds only two pick-up messages ending 14:32:20, before the 14:36:54 deviation, the trip record's messages_during_trip is empty, and there are no in-app calls or call recordings — so POL-RD-21 notice is not established; but the amount is the same on row (b), so this does not move the figure. The sum is the deviation distance times the per-km rate without surge: 2.30 km x 0.92 SGD = 2.12 SGD, the figure the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-05010, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) itself derives as the excess distance fare.\n\nThe rider asked for the whole 36.30 SGD fare. No row of POL-RD-24 returns a trip fare: the base, distance, time, airport surcharge and platform fee for the 19.7 km the rider would have travelled in any event are not disturbed, so the whole-fare claim fails and no larger sum is invented. The driver's submission that the extra travel was one bounded 2.30 km change rather than a whole-ride detour is accepted; it does not change the sum.\n\nOn escalation: the contested amount of 36.30 SGD sits in POL-GEN-22's 10.00–50.00 band, so a ruling stands at 0.80 confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag (rider 0, driver 0), so the 0.95 uplift does not apply; POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is held unapplied because ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false in the loaded policy. Every artifact the matrix needs is complete at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged. Confidence is 0.90.\n\nOutcome: a PARTIAL_REFUND of 2.12 SGD to the rider; the balance of the metered fare stands as charged.",
